Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:11:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] tabletmanager: leave deferred replication to the retry
 after an offline backup
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The cleanup of an offline backup repoints replication to the shard record's
primary without the shard lock. While replication initialization was
deferred, setReplicationSourceLocked started replication even though the
cleanup passes forceStartReplication=false, so it could start a receiver
that a reparent had stopped, from a primary that the reparent was
replacing. It also recorded that primary as the chosen source, so the
retry then waited for it.

Start replication for a pending deferral only in the SetReplicationSource
RPC, and make the cleanup restore the tablet type and leave replication to
the retry while a deferral is pending.

Signed-off-by: Miguel Ángel Pastor Olivar <migue@planetscale.com>
